{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>אשר קרך.</b> From the root of כל הקורות אותם (all who encounter them)." "<b>ויזנב בך.</b> He cut off your tail, and they are the stragglers behind you who had no strength to walk. And it is possible that the word נחשלים is like נחלשים (the weakened ones), and likewise כבש — כשב." "<b>ואתה עיף.</b> For it came at Rephidim, and the people were thirsty for water, as it is written." "<b>ויגע.</b> From the journey." "<b>ולא ירא.</b> Return to Amalek, and it is a transitive verb, like 'for he is heavier than you' (Genesis 13:13), 'for Isaac was old' (Genesis 27:1), 'as he loved' (Genesis 22:2)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {4 "Ibn Ezra quotes phrase fragments to illustrate transitive verb usage; the verse references are inferred from Genesis passages where these forms appear."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:50.892781524Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}